<div id="S4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Cross-method (leave-<math id="S4.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>-method-out).</span>
Holding the source-pair-disjoint resplit fixed, we partition
EVAFusion’s <math id="S4.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="11" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>11</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">11</annotation></semantics></math> fusion methods into five disjoint folds and
re-train FuScore (single seed <math id="S4.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="42" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>42</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">42</annotation></semantics></math>) per fold on the remaining
methods. Tab. <a href="#S4.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 4.3 Out-of-Distribution Generalization via Cross-Method and Cross-Dataset ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Bringing Multimodal Large Language Models to Infrared-Visible Image Fusion Quality Assessment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> reports per-fold and
macro-mean correlation. Macro-mean SRCC is <math id="S4.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.628" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.628</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.628</annotation></semantics></math>, only <math id="S4.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.020" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.020</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.020</annotation></semantics></math>
below the in-distribution 3-seed ensemble; PLCC and KRCC show
comparable <math id="S4.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sim\!2\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sim\!2\%</annotation></semantics></math> absolute drops; per-fold variance is
small (macro-std SRCC <math id="S4.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="=0.004" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>0.004</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">=0.004</annotation></semantics></math>). PairAcc rises under leave-out evaluation as an artefact of restricting source pairs to <math id="S4.SS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|K|\!\in\!\{2,3\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|K|\!\in\!\{2,3\}</annotation></semantics></math> methods
(PairAcc enumerates <math id="S4.SS3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leq 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leq 3</annotation></semantics></math> pairs per source pair instead of
<math id="S4.SS3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\binom{11}{2}{=}55" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac linethickness="0pt"><mn>11</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>55</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\binom{11}{2}{=}55</annotation></semantics></math>); SRCC / PLCC / KRCC are the relevant
cross-method metrics.</p>
</div>
