<section id="A1.SS7" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.7 </span>Inference Cost</h3>

<div id="A1.SS7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The SRCC gain reported in Sec. <a href="#S4.SS2" title="4.2 Main Results ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Bringing Multimodal Large Language Models to Infrared-Visible Image Fusion Quality Assessment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a> comes at a
non-trivial inference cost relative to the in-domain ViT-L+MLP
baseline. Tab. <a href="#A1.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ A.7 Inference Cost ‣ Appendix A Experimental Setup Details ‣ Bringing Multimodal Large Language Models to Infrared-Visible Image Fusion Quality Assessment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> measures per-image latency on
a single NVIDIA A100-80G under batch size <math id="A1.SS7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>, fp16/bf16 native
execution, with the first <math id="A1.SS7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>10</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10</annotation></semantics></math> forwards used as warmup before
the timed window of <math id="A1.SS7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>100</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">100</annotation></semantics></math> test images. The single-seed
configuration incurs a <math id="A1.SS7.p1.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="5.55\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>5.55</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5.55\times</annotation></semantics></math> wall-clock premium over
ViT-L+MLP (<math id="A1.SS7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="276.3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>276.3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">276.3</annotation></semantics></math> vs <math id="A1.SS7.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="49.8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>49.8</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">49.8</annotation></semantics></math> ms median), and the 3-seed ensemble
adds a further <math id="A1.SS7.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="2.17\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2.17</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2.17\times</annotation></semantics></math> to reach <math id="A1.SS7.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="599.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>599.1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">599.1</annotation></semantics></math> ms per image. The
ensemble cost is <em id="A1.SS7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">sub-linear</em> in seed count – <math id="A1.SS7.p1.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="2.17\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2.17</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2.17\times</annotation></semantics></math>
rather than the naive <math id="A1.SS7.p1.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="3\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3\times</annotation></semantics></math> – because per-image data
preparation (image load, processor invocation, device transfer)
amortises across the three sequential adapter forwards rather
than from any cross-adapter compute reuse; under each adapter
the vision encoder and LM transformer fully re-execute.
Decomposing the three measurements algebraically yields a
per-image preparation cost of <math id="A1.SS7.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sim\!115" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∼</mo><mn>115</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sim\!115</annotation></semantics></math> ms and a per-forward
LoRA cost of <math id="A1.SS7.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sim\!162" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∼</mo><mn>162</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sim\!162</annotation></semantics></math> ms, so the ensemble is
<math id="A1.SS7.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="115+3\cdot 162\approx 601" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>115</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>162</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mn>601</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">115+3\cdot 162\approx 601</annotation></semantics></math> ms, matching the observed
<math id="A1.SS7.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="599" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>599</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">599</annotation></semantics></math> ms, whereas independent per-forward prep would give
<math id="A1.SS7.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3\cdot 276=828" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>276</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>828</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3\cdot 276=828</annotation></semantics></math> ms. The LoRA wrapper itself adds a
measurable but modest <math id="A1.SS7.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+79" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>79</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+79</annotation></semantics></math> ms over the bare Qwen3-VL-8B
zero-shot path (<math id="A1.SS7.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="276.3-196.9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>276.3</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>196.9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">276.3-196.9</annotation></semantics></math>). At a per-SRCC-point cost
premium of <math id="A1.SS7.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sim 2.7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∼</mo><mn>2.7</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sim 2.7</annotation></semantics></math> ms per <math id="A1.SS7.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+0.001" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>0.001</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+0.001</annotation></semantics></math> SRCC (single-seed vs
ViT-L+MLP), the trade-off is favourable for offline IQA where
rank quality matters more than latency. Real-time deployment
would call for a smaller MLLM backbone (e.g. Qwen3-VL-2B,
Phi-3.5-vision) and we leave such a cost–quality study to
future work.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.T6" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 6: </span>Per-image inference latency on the EVAFusion test split
(<math id="A1.T6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=100" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=100</annotation></semantics></math> images, single NVIDIA A100-80G, batch size <math id="A1.T6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>,
fp16/bf16 native execution, <math id="A1.T6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>10</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10</annotation></semantics></math> warmup forwards before timing).
Lower is better. “Params” reports total loaded parameters
including all attached adapters.</figcaption>
