<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Extended Ablation Studies</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This appendix extends the loss-composition and
<math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math>-stratification ablations of Sec. <a href="#S4.SS4" title="4.4 Ablation Studies and Further Analysis ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Bringing Multimodal Large Language Models to Infrared-Visible Image Fusion Quality Assessment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.4</span></a>
with: (i) full loss-grid and calibration tables including the
<math id="A2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>-blind-PL diagnostic rows, (ii) the
<math id="A2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="11" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>11</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">11</annotation></semantics></math>-method version of the <math id="A2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math>-stratified analysis, (iii)
the alternative listwise scope (PL on the level distribution),
(iv) the counterfactual SRCC ceiling, (v) the
<math id="A2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>-sensitivity sweep, and (vi) the tertile boundary
choice.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Full Loss-Composition Grid and <math id="A2.SS1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>-blind-PL
Diagnostic</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Tab. <a href="#A2.T7" title="Table 7 ‣ B.1 Full Loss-Composition Grid and 𝜎-blind-PL Diagnostic ‣ Appendix B Extended Ablation Studies ‣ Bringing Multimodal Large Language Models to Infrared-Visible Image Fusion Quality Assessment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> extends the
<math id="A2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math>-row loss-composition panel of
Tab. <a href="#S4.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ 4.4 Ablation Studies and Further Analysis ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Bringing Multimodal Large Language Models to Infrared-Visible Image Fusion Quality Assessment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> with two single-seed diagnostic
configurations that stack a <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>-blind Plackett–Luce
listwise term on top of the <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>-conflict base or our final
composition. Tab. <a href="#A2.T8" title="Table 8 ‣ B.1 Full Loss-Composition Grid and 𝜎-blind-PL Diagnostic ‣ Appendix B Extended Ablation Studies ‣ Bringing Multimodal Large Language Models to Infrared-Visible Image Fusion Quality Assessment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> reports the
corresponding calibration and predicted-<math id="A2.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\sigma}</annotation></semantics></math> statistics
for all five cells.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.T7" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 7: </span>Full loss-composition ablation on EVAFusion test
(<math id="A2.T7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=935" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>935</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=935</annotation></semantics></math> images, <math id="A2.T7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="85" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>85</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">85</annotation></semantics></math> source pairs). Higher is better for all
metrics. Columns match Tab. <a href="#S4.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 4.2 Main Results ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Bringing Multimodal Large Language Models to Infrared-Visible Image Fusion Quality Assessment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>. <span id="A2.T7.15" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Bold</span>
marks the best in each column. <sup id="A2.T7.16" class="ltx_sup"><span id="A2.T7.16.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">†</span></sup> single-seed result;
remaining rows are 3-seed ensembles. <sup id="A2.T7.17" class="ltx_sup"><span id="A2.T7.17.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">‡</span></sup> the
“Ours <math id="A2.T7.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>+</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="A2.T7.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>-blind PL” row stacks an additional listwise
term on top of our final composition; it is reported as a
diagnostic rather than a clean grid cell.</figcaption>
