<figure id="A2.T8" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 8: </span>Calibration and predicted-<math id="A2.T8.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo mathsize="1.110em">^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\sigma}</annotation></semantics></math> statistics on
EVAFusion test (<math id="A2.T8.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=935" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>935</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=935</annotation></semantics></math>). <math id="A2.T8.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{ECE}_{\tau^{\ast}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ECE</mi><msup><mi>τ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{ECE}_{\tau^{\ast}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the
coverage ECE after a single-parameter <math id="A2.T8.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau^{\ast}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>τ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau^{\ast}</annotation></semantics></math> rescaling fit
on one <math id="A2.T8.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="50\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>50</mn><mo mathsize="1.110em">%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">50\%</annotation></semantics></math> cal split (single-split variance <math id="A2.T8.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sim\!0.005" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>∼</mo><mn>0.005</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sim\!0.005</annotation></semantics></math>).
<math id="A2.T8.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{ECE}_{\mathrm{smooth}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ECE</mi><mi>smooth</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{ECE}_{\mathrm{smooth}}</annotation></semantics></math> and the oracle slope <math id="A2.T8.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b^{\ast}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b^{\ast}</annotation></semantics></math>
are averaged across <math id="A2.T8.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>50</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">50</annotation></semantics></math> Monte-Carlo cal/test splits;
<math id="A2.T8.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b^{\ast}\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b^{\ast}\to 0</annotation></semantics></math> indicates that single-<math id="A2.T8.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau^{\ast}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>τ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau^{\ast}</annotation></semantics></math> scaling is the
optimal recalibrator. The last two columns report the mean of
the predicted <math id="A2.T8.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo mathsize="1.110em">^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\sigma}</annotation></semantics></math> and its Pearson correlation with the
per-image dimensional conflict <math id="A2.T8.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. <span id="A2.T8.26" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Bold</span> marks
the best in each ECE column and the largest
<math id="A2.T8.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho(\hat{\sigma}_{i},\delta_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo mathsize="1.110em">^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho(\hat{\sigma}_{i},\delta_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>. <sup id="A2.T8.27" class="ltx_sup"><span id="A2.T8.27.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">†</span></sup> single-seed result;
remaining rows are 3-seed ensembles. <sup id="A2.T8.28" class="ltx_sup"><span id="A2.T8.28.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">‡</span></sup> diagnostic
row stacking a <math id="A2.T8.m35" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>-blind listwise term on top of our final
composition. External baselines do not predict <math id="A2.T8.m36" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo mathsize="1.110em">^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\sigma}</annotation></semantics></math> and
are omitted.</figcaption>
