<section id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph"><math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>-blind Plackett–Luce ranking inflates
<math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\sigma}</annotation></semantics></math> and degrades calibration.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Two configurations isolate the failure mode of <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>-blind
ranking on a <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>-conflict-supervised model. First,
replacing the <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>-aware Thurstone term with a
<math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>-blind Plackett–Luce listwise term on the same
<math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>-conflict base regresses SRCC by <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-0.0080" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>0.0080</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-0.0080</annotation></semantics></math>
(Tab. <a href="#A2.T7" title="Table 7 ‣ B.1 Full Loss-Composition Grid and 𝜎-blind-PL Diagnostic ‣ Appendix B Extended Ablation Studies ‣ Bringing Multimodal Large Language Models to Infrared-Visible Image Fusion Quality Assessment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>: <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.6477\to 0.6397" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.6477</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0.6397</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.6477\to 0.6397</annotation></semantics></math>). Second,
stacking <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>-blind PL <em id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">on top of</em> our final
composition lowers SRCC by <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.0050" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.0050</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.0050</annotation></semantics></math> and substantially worsens
calibration (Tab. <a href="#A2.T8" title="Table 8 ‣ B.1 Full Loss-Composition Grid and 𝜎-blind-PL Diagnostic ‣ Appendix B Extended Ablation Studies ‣ Bringing Multimodal Large Language Models to Infrared-Visible Image Fusion Quality Assessment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>:
<math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{ECE}_{\tau^{\ast}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ECE</mi><msup><mi>τ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{ECE}_{\tau^{\ast}}</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.022\to 0.032" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.022</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0.032</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.022\to 0.032</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{ECE}_{\mathrm{smooth}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ECE</mi><mi>smooth</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{ECE}_{\mathrm{smooth}}</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.021\to 0.027" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0.021</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0.027</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.021\to 0.027</annotation></semantics></math>). The
mechanism is consistent across both cells: the <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>-blind
listwise gradient broadens the predicted distribution to satisfy
global rank ordering, inflating <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\sigma}</annotation></semantics></math>’s mean by
<math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.06" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.06</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.06</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.13" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.13</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.13</annotation></semantics></math> over the corresponding non-PL cell (reaching
<math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.82" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.82</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.82</annotation></semantics></math> in the diagnostic stack – the largest value in
Tab. <a href="#A2.T8" title="Table 8 ‣ B.1 Full Loss-Composition Grid and 𝜎-blind-PL Diagnostic ‣ Appendix B Extended Ablation Studies ‣ Bringing Multimodal Large Language Models to Infrared-Visible Image Fusion Quality Assessment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>). Single-parameter
recalibration cannot absorb this <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\sigma}</annotation></semantics></math>-dependent
inflation, which is why <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b^{\ast}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>b</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b^{\ast}</annotation></semantics></math> shifts from <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> to
<math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+0.30" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>0.30</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+0.30</annotation></semantics></math>–<math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+0.53" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>0.53</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+0.53</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{ECE}_{\mathrm{smooth}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ECE</mi><mi>smooth</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{ECE}_{\mathrm{smooth}}</annotation></semantics></math> rises in
both PL-augmented rows. The <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>-aware Thurstone term, by
contrast, leaves <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\sigma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>σ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\sigma}</annotation></semantics></math>’s mean within <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.04" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.04</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.04</annotation></semantics></math> of the
<math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>-conflict-only configuration – the structural reason it
preserves calibration where <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>-blind ranking does not.
<math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>-blind ranking therefore provides no calibration benefit
on a <math id="A2.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>-supervised base and actively hurts it.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Eleven-Method <math id="A2.SS2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math>-Stratified Analysis</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Tab. <a href="#A2.T9" title="Table 9 ‣ B.2 Eleven-Method 𝛿-Stratified Analysis ‣ Appendix B Extended Ablation Studies ‣ Bringing Multimodal Large Language Models to Infrared-Visible Image Fusion Quality Assessment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> reports per-tertile SRCC
for all <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="11" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>11</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">11</annotation></semantics></math> scoring methods referenced in
Sec. <a href="#S4.SS4" title="4.4 Ablation Studies and Further Analysis ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Bringing Multimodal Large Language Models to Infrared-Visible Image Fusion Quality Assessment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.4</span></a>, extending the <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math>-row
representative panel of Tab. <a href="#S4.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ 4.4 Ablation Studies and Further Analysis ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Bringing Multimodal Large Language Models to Infrared-Visible Image Fusion Quality Assessment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> (right)
with the remaining handcrafted statistics (VIF, MI), the
zero-shot natural-image MLLM-IQA scorer Q-Align, and the four
remaining loss-composition cells. The high-<math id="A2.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> column
exhibits the same data-side floor pattern claimed in the main
text: SRCC across all <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="11" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>11</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">11</annotation></semantics></math> methods collapses into the band
<math id="A2.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0.140,0.254]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0.140</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.254</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0.140,0.254]</annotation></semantics></math> on this tertile.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.T9" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 9: </span>SRCC stratified by per-image dimensional conflict
<math id="A2.T9.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> across <math id="A2.T9.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="11" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>11</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">11</annotation></semantics></math> scoring methods on the EVAFusion test
set (<math id="A2.T9.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=935" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>935</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=935</annotation></semantics></math>). <math id="A2.T9.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is the standard deviation of the
four sub-dimension scores per image
(§<a href="#S3.SS2" title="3.2 Sub-Dimension-Aware Soft Label Construction ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ Bringing Multimodal Large Language Models to Infrared-Visible Image Fusion Quality Assessment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>); higher <math id="A2.T9.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> indicates
greater dimensional disagreement. Tertile boundaries chosen as
described in App. <a href="#A2.SS3" title="B.3 Tertile Boundary Choice ‣ Appendix B Extended Ablation Studies ‣ Bringing Multimodal Large Language Models to Infrared-Visible Image Fusion Quality Assessment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.3</span></a>, yielding
<math id="A2.T9.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=468/218/249" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>468</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>218</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>249</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=468/218/249</annotation></semantics></math>. <span id="A2.T9.19" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Bold</span> marks the best score per
column across all <math id="A2.T9.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="11" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>11</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">11</annotation></semantics></math> methods. <sup id="A2.T9.20" class="ltx_sup"><span id="A2.T9.20.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">†</span></sup> single-seed result;
remaining ablation rows are 3-seed ensembles. <sup id="A2.T9.21" class="ltx_sup"><span id="A2.T9.21.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">‡</span></sup>
diagnostic stack on top of our final composition.</figcaption>
<table id="A2.T9.22" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A2.T9.22.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A2.T9.22.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:5.0pt;padding-right:5.0pt;"></th>
<th id="A2.T9.22.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:5.0pt;padding-right:5.0pt;"><span id="A2.T9.22.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Method</span></th>
<td id="A2.T9.22.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:5.0pt;padding-right:5.0pt;"><span id="A2.T9.22.1.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">low-<math id="A2.T9.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math></span></td>
<td id="A2.T9.22.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:5.0pt;padding-right:5.0pt;"><span id="A2.T9.22.1.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">mid-<math id="A2.T9.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math></span></td>
<td id="A2.T9.22.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:5.0pt;padding-right:5.0pt;"><span id="A2.T9.22.1.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">high-<math id="A2.T9.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math></span></td>
